Follow-up to the Origin check: the server has a built-in allowlist (loopback origins on any port) and a SetAllowedOrigins hook, but no config field. Anyone serving a browser-based MCP client from a non-loopback origin has no way to allow it. Acceptance: an mcp.allowedOrigins list in the config, wired through main.go to SetAllowedOrigins, documented in README and unreagent.example.yaml, covered by a config test; internal/config territory, which is why the worker deferred it.
